What about a zone where standard time only occurs in a narrow window not at month starts? E.g., a zone with DST from Jan 15 to Dec 15, standard Dec 15-Jan 15. Then Jan 1 = standard, so covered. If DST from Jan 2 to Dec 30, standard Dec 30-Jan 2. Jan 1 standard → covered. Only if the standard window is entirely within a month and doesn't include the 1st. Extremely unlikely historically.

